WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.570
A weekday afternoon on the underground.

2
00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.280
The carriage is busy.

3
00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.980
A man stumbles, and falls to the floor.

4
00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:10.020
In this version, he's
carrying a walking cane.

5
00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:10.960
Rewind.

6
00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.030
Same man, same fall.

7
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.040
This time he's holding
a bottle in a paper bag.

8
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.920
Everyone is looking at him.

9
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.380
Does what he's carrying
change who steps in to help?

10
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.990
In this mission, you'll study bystanders:

11
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.700
people who see an emergency
but are not directly involved.

12
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:32.140
You'll weigh up what helping can cost,
and ask whether a crowd makes each person

13
00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:33.920
feel less responsible.

14
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.150
And you'll find out why some people
are more likely to help than others.

15
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:43.310
Your mission: work out whether a cane
or a bottle changes who helps, and why.
